  "term": "law of constancy",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, the law of constancy refers to the mind’s capacity to intend or mean the same thing again across different moments, even if the actual object or world may have changed. It describes a subjective feature of thought that lets us recognize identity and repeated experience by using the notion of sameness in our meanings.",
